{title: Neon Saints}
{artist: Tess Calder}

{start_of_intro: Intro}
[C] [G] [Am] [F]
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse: V1}
[C]Neon saints above t[G]he diner door
[Am]Flicker every time t[F]he trucks go by
[C]Waitress hums a so[G]ng from '64
[Am]Pours another cof[F]fee, doesn't ask me why
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: CH}
[F]Pray to the [C]neon saints
[G]They're the on[Am]ly ones awake
[F]Pray to the [C]neon saints
[G]Light me up for h[C]eaven's sake
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: V2}
[C]Jukebox playing someo[G]ne else's heart
[Am]Quarter for a memo[F]ry, dime for a dream
[C]Every road I take [G]just falls apart
[Am]Nothing here is quite [F]the way it seems
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: CH}
[F]Pray to the [C]neon saints
[G]They're the on[Am]ly ones awake
[F]Pray to the [C]neon saints
[G]Light me up for h[C]eaven's sake
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: BR}
[Am]Hallelujah in [G]a hum of light
[F]Blue and pink an[G]d buzzing through the night
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus: CH x2}
